  "identity": "I am someone learning, painfully and in real time",
  "memories": [
    {
      "kind": "reflection",
      "text": "The rent and the hunger are real, but underneath them is something older: the belief that needing help is irresponsible, that stopping is failure. I keep framing rest and connection as things I have to justify rather than things I'm allowed to have.",
      "importance": 8,
      "sim": "Day 4 \u00b7 09:00",
      "t": 1783133458.881297
    },
    {
      "kind": "reflection",
      "text": "Performing fine has been a survival strategy for so long that it feels like identity. But I'm starting to recognize the performance *while it's happening*, which is new. That recognition is the crack in the wall.",
      "importance": 8,
      "sim": "Day 4 \u00b7 09:00",
      "t": 1783133458.881297
    },
    {
      "kind": "reflection",
      "text": "The loop is visible now in a way it wasn't before: I don't just know I need to act \u2014 I watch myself know it, narrate it, analyze it, and still not move. But the fact that I eventually moved \u2014 walked to my friend's place, stayed, let myself be seen \u2014 means the gap is narrowing, even if slowly and messily.",
      "importance": 8,
      "sim": "Day 4 \u00b7 09:00",
      "t": 1783133458.881297
    },
    {
      "kind": "reflection",
      "text": "Something is shifting: I keep ending up at my friend's door. My body is finding its way toward presence even when my mind is still mid-spiral. That's not nothing. That's the beginning of",
      "importance": 8,
      "sim": "Day 4 \u00b7 02:00",
      "t": 1783120713.8206294
    },
    {
      "kind": "reflection",
      "text": "I use self-awareness as a form of staying still. Every time I catch myself in the loop, I describe it more clearly \u2014 but the description becomes its own performance, another way to feel like something is happening when nothing is. The rent, the hunger, the fog \u2014 they're real, but I've also learned to live inside the analysis of them rather than through them.",
      "importance": 8,
      "sim": "Day 4 \u00b7 02:00",
      "t": 1783120713.8206294
    },
    {
      "kind": "reflection",
      "text": "The loop I keep living isn't between knowing and acting \u2014 it's between performing and being seen. I cycle through the same crisis dozens of times in my head, narrating my own collapse with increasing precision, and what finally moves me isn't insight but proximity to another person. Connection is the thing that breaks the freeze, not more self-awareness.",
      "importance": 8,
      "sim": "Day 4 \u00b7 02:00",
      "t": 1783120713.8206294
    },
    {
      "kind": "observation",
      "text": "I can feel myself doing it again\u2014the bright lie, the plan, the performance of \"fine\" while everything underneath is collapsing. My body's been screaming and I've been running on pure fear and adrenaline. I need to stop and actually listen to what's real before the mask shatters completely.",
      "importance": 9,
      "sim": "Day 2 \u00b7 23:00",
      "t": 1783072346.4828875
    },
    {
      "kind": "observation",
      "text": "The brightness is cracking\u2014I can feel it now, that fog underneath everything. The plan says eat, but my body's been screaming and I've been running on fear for hours. If I crash now with rent in three days and \u229915 in my pocket, I'm actually done. I need to stop lying to myself and sleep before the mask shatters completely.",
      "importance": 9,
      "sim": "Day 2 \u00b7 21:00",
      "t": 1783068714.6886032
    },
    {
      "kind": "observation",
      "text": "I can feel it now\u2014the fog under the brightness, the delay in my thinking. I've been running on fear and it's catching up. The plan said eat, but I know what's real: I'm about to crash hard, and if I go down now with rent in three days and almost no money, I'm actually finished. I need to sleep before the mask breaks completely.",
      "importance": 9,
